---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Src from '../components/Src.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="Why the Galamsey Tracker exists and where to report illegal mining in Ghana.">
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>Galamsey is gold mining without a licence. It strips forest, digs pits that fill with water and turns rivers brown with mud. In 2022 the Daboase water treatment plant on the River Pra, which supplies Sekondi-Takoradi, could run only about two hours a day because its intake was choked with silt, and the city had been on water rationing for three years.</p>
    <p>The Galamsey Tracker shows where land is being cleared, week by week, using only free satellite data from NASA and the European Union's <Src id="copernicus">Copernicus programme</Src>. Nobody has to visit a site or file a report for it to appear here. The aim is that anyone, from a reporter to a district officer to someone who lives nearby, can see the same evidence and check it.</p>
    <p>It is an independent project by an ordinary citizen who cares about the problem, not a scientist or a mining expert. It relies on data and methods published by NASA and the European Space Agency, and <a href="/method">explains how it works</a> so anyone can check it. It is not connected to the government or any company.</p>
    <h2>Report illegal mining</h2>
    <p>This site cannot take reports or act on them. If you see illegal mining, you can report it to the <Src id="minerals-commission">Minerals Commission</Src> or to the National Anti-Illegal Mining Operations Secretariat, NAIMOS. You can also tell your District Assembly.</p>

    {CONTACT_EMAIL && (
      <>
        <h2>Get in touch</h2>
        <p>For questions about the data, corrections or press enquiries, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. A person reads every message.</p>
      </>
    )}
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: calc(68ch + 2 * var(--gutter)); padding-bottom: 24px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.4vw, 2.5rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 32px 0 20px; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.375rem; margin: 36px 0 10px; }
  p { margin: 0 0 14px; }
</style>
